@node Agents and Sling
@chapter Agents and Sling
@anchor{agents}
@cindex agents
@cindex sling
@cindex sessions

beads.el can launch an AI agent on an issue from inside Emacs.  A
@emph{session} is the combination of an agent @emph{type} (what the agent
is asked to do) and a @emph{backend} (the program and terminal that run
it), optionally isolated in a git worktree.  Sessions are tracked in an
in-house registry, so no external session-manager package is required.

